From 24091e422a432bb9081c89aaf8e4a68ac6818710 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 02:38:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A prayer pressed while you are busy is queued, not thrown
 away

Reported from play as "prayer activation has bad delays". A prayer button is
run unprotected - IfButtonHandler passes protect = root.overlay == false and
the prayer tab is an overlay - so the script has to take protected access with
p_finduid(uid). That calls canAccess(), which is !protect && !busy(), and
busy() is delayed || containsModalInterface. Press a prayer during a spec, a
teleport or a skilling swing and it failed, fell through to a bare varp resync,
and the orb the client had already lit flicked straight back off. No message,
no retry, nothing.

A queue gets protected access AND only runs once canAccess() is true again, so
the press now survives the delay and the prayer comes on the moment it ends.
The button is buttontype=toggle with pushvar, so the client flips the varp on
every press; queueing one toggle per press keeps the parity the player can see,
and the activate label writes the varp itself, which is the resync that used to
be done by hand.

WHAT THIS DELIBERATELY DOES NOT CHANGE: whether praying interrupts what you
were doing. I was about to delete the p_clearpendingaction from all eighteen
scripts - it is half of "actions get cancelled for doing anything" - and found
that clarity.rs2 cites THREE pieces of period footage for it. Upstream watched
2006 video and concluded a prayer does stop you. My argument for removing it
was 1-tick prayer flicking, which is a modern OSRS technique and proves nothing
about this era. So it stays, it is pinned by a check, and whether to diverge
from upstream there is Corey's call rather than a tidy-up.

The investigation behind all of this is claude/combat-delays-investigation.md:
four mechanisms, all four inherited from upstream LostCityRS (I cloned both
repos and diffed - the engine handler is identical and the prayer script was
byte-identical), and two of them engine changes that cannot be built or tested
in the cloud.

combat_battery group 4, six mutations, each caught by its own check. rs2check
0 ERROR 0 CHECK, selftest PASS, eleven batteries ALL PASS. Not compiled: npm is
still 403ing zod.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Dc7giZ7Qnh4qy1CYPTDrmH
